Z||000000||swoods||08-15-2001||07:30 PM||||I currently own a 1984 2m4 runs really good I wanted to go ahead and restore and give a good rebuild on the motor which will give me about 135 horse power. Well today I was out looking for a wing for my car and I came across a broken down 85 gt in alright shape lots of good parts well by the time I was done I was buying the car I got it really cheap I knew I could use the wing and the seats and the dash are in perfect shape and the sunroof is perfect to the body is in alright shape. The only bad thing is the motor as a cracked rod. My biggest problem is should I keep the gt and fix it or should I take what I need of the car and then part the rest. I'm going crazy here please help I would like all your suggestions.  ||||reg||1
Z||000001||Elenor84||08-15-2001||08:25 PM||||convert your 84 into a 85 gt...<BR>thats what I"m doing except I'm converting my 84 into a 86...<P>------------------<BR>Lance<BR>Click Image to go to site.<BR><A HREF="http://members.nbci.com/_XMCM/lancegspage/Index.html" TARGET=_blank> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/Side1.jpg"> </A>||||reg||1
Z||000002||starfighter007@msn.com||08-15-2001||08:29 PM||||sorry this is your decsion to figure out  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/confused.gif">But if it were me I would agree with Elenor84||||reg||1
Z||000003||rockcrawl||08-15-2001||08:38 PM||||First of all you need to buy a few more broken Fieros. Don't stop looking until you have four or five of them sitting in your driveway/yard. That's what I do. You gotta have choices.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif">||||reg||1
Z||000004||fix||08-15-2001||08:49 PM||||I agree with rockcrawl.  I only own 2 fieros right now (one parts car), but I'm always looking to expand the fleet with some parts cars.  But seriously, I think I would either convert your 84 to an 85 GT or fix the GT.  I think you are being unrealistic about getting 135 horse from a duke.  If you can actually acomplish that then the motor won't be long for this world.  Duke's are not meant to be built up.  You're better off rebuilding the 2.8 out of the GT or finding another 60 degree V6 that's plug and play.  just my opinion||||reg||1
Z||000005||Tigger||08-15-2001||09:51 PM||||Hmmm... I restored my '84 SE.  Didn't have to decide between it and a GT.  I think I would try to either rebuild or get a new engine for the GT, especially if the rest is salvageable.  Get it running and then you'll have one as an everyday Fiero and one you can pamper.<P>The GT will hold more value in the end and you won't be stepping on anyone's toes if you know what I mean.   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><P>------------------<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/tiggerblue4.gif"> <BR>T-T-F-N, Ta Ta For Now!<BR><A HREF="http://www.fortunecity.com/tatooine/spielberg/241/" TARGET=_blank>Tigger's Fiero Page</A>||||reg||1
