Z||000018||Elvira||08-19-2001||10:17 AM||||Look at it this way:  You already own them so it isn't like you have to pay monthly on them.  Cover one and work on the other at you leisure, tnen work on the other.  That is what we are doing with ours.  We have Chester's show 86GT, then we have another 86black GT that I was going to fix up, but it needs lots of work so I found a blue 87GT for cheap that needs a motor that I am fixing and the ohther black has now become our V8 donor, we also have an 86 coupe with t-tops that just needs seals and brakes AND we are going to WI next weekend to pick up a 4-seater Fiero.  Point of this is you don't need to decide on this one or that one, just do both, so it takes some time.  Enjoy!!<BR><P>------------------<BR>Elvira<BR>Blue 87GT<BR>Black 86GT 5sp x 2<BR>86SC t-top 58k miles||||reg||10
